      "claim": "Mianserin, a tetracyclic antidepressant with an N-methylated ring system, showed a logBB of 0.99, indicating good brain penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query molecule (protopine) is a lipophilic protoberberine-type alkaloid with two methylenedioxy groups and a tertiary amine. Multiple structurally related alkaloids—tetrahydroberberine, berberrubine, coptisine, apomorphine, and nuciferine—demonstrate robust BBB penetration in rodents and primates. No contradictory evidence was found. Therefore, meaningful CNS access is expected.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct pharmacokinetic or BBB data for protopine itself were provided; the prediction relies on strong structural analogy to related protoberberine alkaloids.",
    "The query contains a carbonyl group that is absent in the closest analogues, which could slightly alter permeability, but this is not expected to negate the class-level CNS access."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

